      "parents": [
        {
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/f5e10868da4442cee68e117f259880753b36d86c",
          "sha": "f5e10868da4442cee68e117f259880753b36d86c",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/f5e10868da4442cee68e117f259880753b36d86c"
        }
      ],
      "message": "net: ignore privacy-network peers' view of our address\n\n- if i make an outbound connection to a tor/i2p peer\n\tme ---------> tor peer\n  in the VERSION message the tor peer sends us back,\n  there's a field which tells us about the address\n  the peer thinks we are (addrMe) that can be used for\n  self advertisement. Peers in privacy networks can't\n  know this. So they send [::]:0.\n\n  if a peer sends us a routable ipv4 address instead\n  of [::]:0 - make sure to ignore it.\n\n  if we don't ignore it, we can end up sending them\n  as self advertisement the routable ipv4 address\n  they sent us and our listening port. ignoring it\n  will help prevent our custom clearnet port leaks\n  to privacy networks.",
